  "sourceQualifications": [
    "CAGR comment says strictly positive endpoints; executable branch accepts ending zero and returns -100%. Card describes that nonnegative-ending convention without modifying engine code.",
    "Period change divides by absolute prior; differs from signed-prior division for negative bases.",
    "CV source uses sample SD / absolute mean; card identifies the convention and limits interpretation.",
    "Mid-rank uses half of exact ties; card displays percent while source returns a fraction.",
    "Second batch combines original ST13 Z-score and ST14 IQR candidate scopes in S-013; S-014 is the newly requested winsorization concept W01. This replaces one freed planning slot without automatically increasing the original 64-additional-card baseline.",
    "S-015 teaches sample covariance used internally by Pearson correlation; the portfolio covariance service is a throwing Phase 2+ scaffold and remains unimplemented.",
    "S-016 extends comparability with an original count-weighted pooled-mean example for disjoint groups; geography.ts wraps identities and does not implement this pooled estimator or a spatial join.",
    "S-017 uses illustrative supplied weights, not E87 default hierarchy/freshness/comparability weights; no current benchmark, confidence interval or deployed consensus service is claimed.",
    "S-018 completeness is a field-presence illustration, not the engine composite quality score; source reliability must be externally established, missing evidence is not manufactured."
  ]
